    "result_text": "The build is green: **BUILD SUCCESS**, 68 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors.\n\n## Summary\n\nI unified `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` into a single `memberId` formatted `'<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>'`, and removed the standalone `checkDigit` field.\n\n**Format** (e.g. `NSW26F0AA8C974`): region code + 2-digit fiscal year + 8 upper-hex SHA-256-over-(telephone+lastName) + one Luhn check digit computed over the digits of `<REGION><FY><HASH8>`.\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n- **`AssignMemberId.java`** (renamed from `AssignCustomerCode.java`) \u2014 now builds the full memberId: reuses the existing HASH8, appends the 2-digit FY (from `getFiscalYear()`) and the Luhn CHK, and keeps the collision-dedup loop (`-<n>` suffix) now operating on `memberId`.\n- **`Owner.java`** \u2014 field/column `customerCode`/`customer_code` \u2192 `memberId`/`member_id`; `getPrimaryIdentifier()` returns the memberId; updated docs.\n- **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 removed the `membershipNumber` and `checkDigit` mappings and the now-unused `luhn` helper; `memberId` auto-maps by name.\n- **`AuditOwnerCreated.java`** \u2014 audit line now carries `id`, `registrationDate`, `membershipLevel`, `memberId` (dropped the two removed fields).\n- **`OwnerCreatedEvent.java`** \u2014 structured event's identifier slot renamed to `memberId` in both the record and JSON.\n- **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 pipeline step renamed to `assignMemberId` wiring the new class.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 replaced the `customerCode` schema with `memberId`; removed `membershipNumber` and `checkDigit`.\n- **DB schemas** (h2/hsqldb/mysql/postgres) \u2014 `customer_code` column \u2192 `member_id` (widened to fit the longer id).\n- Cleaned up a stale `AssignCustomerCode` doc reference in `EnsureCityCapacity.java`.\n\nCollision handling, the fiscal-year value, the audit record, and the owner segment all reference the memberId as required.",
